jistanidiot@gmail.com wrote:
>
> So I've died countless times in Sokoban and in the Mines.

Join the club.  If one of my characters survives those then there's an
okay chance I'll get so close to ascending I'll be furious at the
mistake that kills me later.  ;^)

> I'm
> wondering is it really necessary to do these two branches?

Strictly speaking, you can skip the Mines and Sokoban but can
not skip the Quest or Vlad's Tower.

But skipping them is NOT going to help your game *at all*.
Seriously.  It is necessary to learn how to live through them to
be able to survive the rest of the game.  Skip them and you
fail to learn how to survive them.  Fail to learn how to survive
them and you will not survive later.

> Sokoban's
> rewards are nice but I'm sure I can find them elsewhere.

Being sure isn't the same as being correct.  Each level has at
least one guaranteed feature that have low chances of
existing elsewhere in the game.  It would not be surprising to
go an entire game with no replacement for the prize in the
mines, and in Sokoban the guaranteed items other than the
prize are worth the effort of the puzzle.

> Plus half the
> time I usually get killed by a swarm of bees or something before I even
> make it to the zoo.

What lesson do you learn from each death?  Fail to learn a
lesson from each death and it will repeat.  Why did you
*really* die in that case?  Hint - the bees have little to do with
the real reason; the real reason is playing strategy.

> The mines are even worse.

Compared to the unlimited storable food in Sokoban the Mines
supply unlimited eat-now food plus unlimited usefull items.
But the exact same reason that you die in Sokoban applies.
You aren't learning strategy lessons from each death.

> Even if I make it to
> the temple it usually is guarded by an angry priest.

The priest is never angry in a non-bones file.  There are ways to
make a priest angry.  Learn what they are and don't do that.
Then play enough times that the bones level is deleted.  Simple
strategy.

> So do any of you skip both and still win?

Flipping through my memory of ascension posts I can't remember
a single one that didn't include a trip through the mines. And
once you can survive the mines you can survive Sokoban ...

Seriously - learn about retreat, using corners, missiles, burden.
Do that and you won't need to die every time in the mines.

Also, please understand that most players die almost every time
in the mines.  Only very good very seasoned players go into
the mines expecting to survive every time.



